00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:16.570
That's like longer than the Kardashians.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.470
- Thinking back to "Freak
Show" in particular,

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.600
anybody who has watched
the entirety of that season

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.360
knows you get invested for 90% of the show

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.300
just for it not to matter for the last 10.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.860
So, I am always just a little cautious

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.330
when it comes to jumping feet first

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.910
into a season of "American Horror Story,"

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.431
but if I just look at these two episodes,

00:08:33.431 --> 00:08:35.730
solid start, I am hooked.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:36.570
- Solid start, but I agree with you.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.510
It is an emotional journey
and it's a commitment.

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.120
But I want to know from you guys,

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.380
do you think that we're missing anything

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.170
by not having the "American
Horror Story" staples

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.630
like Jessica Lange, Kathy
Bates, Sarah Paulson?

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.200
'Cause you were talking
about message boards

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.830
and I feel like when I
read the message boards,

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.700
a lot of people are kind of bummed

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.630
that they're not in this season.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:55.940
So do you guys think
we're losing anything?

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.050
Do we think they're gonna pop up

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.780
in another episode this season?

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.220
- My money's on Sarah Paulson.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.280
I think during an interview,

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.870
she already admitted she
might pop up at a point,

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:07.410
and, I mean, I think she's
attached to this franchise

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.180
for as long as it lasts.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:12.700
And when it comes to Kathy
Bates and Angela Bassett

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:13.540
and Jessica Lange,

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.400
we're talking about icons
- Yeah.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.340
- in the genre and in
filmmaking and TV shows

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:19.173
across the board.

00:09:19.173 --> 00:09:20.880
Whenever their absence is felt,

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.180
it's gonna hurt a little.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:23.013
- Yeah.

00:09:23.013 --> 00:09:24.070
- I think they will pop up,

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:25.820
maybe just even for a little bit.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.450
I would love for Kathy Bates to pop up,

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:28.770
Just because it kinda seems like--

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:29.935
- Who wouldn't?
- Well, I mean--

00:09:29.935 --> 00:09:30.768
(Naz laughing)

00:09:30.768 --> 00:09:32.727
It seems like they're setting up this

00:09:32.727 --> 00:09:34.240
"Freddy vs. Jason" scenario

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.330
when it comes to Mr. Jingles
versus Richard Ramirez.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.560
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:39.110
- So, in a weird, like,

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:41.010
if I could just take a
villain from another movie,

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.389
I would love for Kathy Bates from "Misery"

00:09:43.389 --> 00:09:44.910
(all laughing)
to pop into this movie.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:45.743
- Oh, wow.

00:09:45.743 --> 00:09:47.070
I'll never say no to Annie Wilkes.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:49.220
- And having a head to head to head

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.300
inside this camp,

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.850
and who really cares about the campers,

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:52.870
just let those three go at it.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:53.703
(Naz laughs)

00:09:53.703 --> 00:09:54.536
I think they'll pop up.

00:09:54.536 --> 00:09:55.426
Sarah Paulson I think will pop up.

00:09:55.426 --> 00:09:56.259
- Yeah.

00:09:56.259 --> 00:09:58.090
- I wonder if part of it, though, is

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:01.100
obviously, Ryan Murphy
loves making this show,

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:03.900
maybe wants to continue to
do it for several more years.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.620
Letting some of the other
cast members kinda--

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:08.460
- Have their day in the sun?

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.200
- Yeah, 'cause like Billie Lourd

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:11.040
is really--

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.019
- [Naz] She's so funny as Montana

00:10:12.019 --> 00:10:13.205
- [Ryan] She's so good.

00:10:13.205 --> 00:10:14.038
- Yeah.

00:10:14.038 --> 00:10:17.080
And I think Emma Roberts has
so much scream queen cred.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:18.700
I mean, she was Sidney Prescott's cousin,

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.677
she was the killer in "Scream 4."

00:10:20.677 --> 00:10:21.510
- [Shane] Love Scream 4.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.640
- I think she

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.070
could literally just take this,

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:25.590
and I personally feel like

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:27.980
we're not gonna see any of
the staples in this season.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.896
- Her performance in "Scream 4"

00:10:29.896 --> 00:10:32.600
(all laughing)
just shows the immense range

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.433
that she has.
- So good.

00:10:33.433 --> 00:10:34.280
- and it's actually
- So good.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.290
- something we can see in
"American Horror Story,"

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:38.100
'cause we've seen her play, you know,

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.640
the straight woman, so to speak,

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:43.530
but also a crazy character
who's super over the top

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:45.870
and sometimes conniving and mean.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.950
- Yeah, I feel like
we're used to seeing her

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:48.890
being conniving and mean,

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.910
and I actually like her
character in "1984."

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:53.660
I like that she's playing
kind of like the opposite

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.862
of what were used to seeing her play.

00:10:54.862 --> 00:10:55.840
- [Perri] That's what you think for now.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:56.673
- [Ryan] I was about to say--

00:10:56.673 --> 00:10:57.760
- Wait until they turn it on its head.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.280
- She is kind of a harbinger
of doom in this series.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.020
Everywhere she goes, the body count rises.

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.700
- Well, it's like that one line

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.780
that Billie Lourd says to her,

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:08.480
where it's something to the effect

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.730
of, "If all you see is the bad,

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:11.563
all you're gonna--"

00:11:11.563 --> 00:11:12.610
- "If all you see is
the shadows, that's all

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.570
that you're gonna see."
- Yes, yes.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:14.403
- Yeah.

00:11:14.403 --> 00:11:16.260
- She basically embodies that.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.650
- [Ryan] To be fair she
did see her future husband

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:19.500
get his head blown off.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:20.540
- Oh, I forgot about.
- You think she saw that.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.520
- And her dad.
- Oh, god.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:24.020
- We don't even necessarily know

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.519
if any of that is 100% true.

00:11:25.519 --> 00:11:26.352
At this point
- That is true.

00:11:26.352 --> 00:11:27.185
- I do think she really
- That's true.

00:11:27.185 --> 00:11:28.090
- went through all of that.

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:29.440
But, you never know.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:30.428
- I love that scene,

00:11:30.428 --> 00:11:32.153
by the way.
- That was a lot.

00:11:32.153 --> 00:11:32.986
- Such a good scene.

00:11:32.986 --> 00:11:35.795
- It's the Red Wedding of
"American Horror Story."

00:11:35.795 --> 00:11:37.160
- Yeah, it was the Ryan
Murphy Red Wedding.

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.570
- It was certainly effective.

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:39.490
- Okay, well one thing we do know--

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:41.854
- (laughs) It was certainly effective.

00:11:41.854 --> 00:11:43.097
These brains were everywhere.
- Shane's like

00:11:43.097 --> 00:11:45.580
"Yeah, that worked for me,
I'm not getting married."

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:47.540
So one thing we do know
is obviously that the '80s

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.200
are heavily influencing the show, right?

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.450
We talked about "Friday the 13th."

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.780
We're also getting Michael Myers-y vibes,

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:55.910
but also there's true
crime from LA in this.

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:57.300
I wanna know from you guys,

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.290
do you think we're gonna
see anymore real life

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:00.940
serial killers in this show?

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:02.670
- I will say I hope not.

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:06.720
And this may be, not to sound
like a wet blanket here,

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.980
but I don't like when people
take real life serial killers

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.946
and be like, "They're
part of the MCU now."

00:12:11.946 --> 00:12:14.110
(all laughing)

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:14.960
- Richard Ramirez is gonna

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:15.890
join the Avengers?
- Yeah, oh,

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:17.913
is the Zodiac gonna come in here too?

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:21.660
Like they're characters
when they're awful people.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:23.260
- [Shane] Richard Ramirez is a monster.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.150
- [Naz] Yeah, I know.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:24.983
- [Shane] Human monster.

00:12:24.983 --> 00:12:27.210
- But he's not that scary to me in "1984,"

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:28.270
but yeah, I think about that too,

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:31.200
because Xavier, the character in "1984,"

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:32.560
mentions Son of Sam

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:33.393
in the first episode.
- Yeah.

00:12:33.393 --> 00:12:34.226
- [Shane] That's true, yeah.

00:12:34.226 --> 00:12:36.304
- And I'm like "I just watched
'Mindhunter,'" you know?

00:12:36.304 --> 00:12:37.270
- [Ryan] He was great in that.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:38.826
- Do they get money or royalties?

00:12:38.826 --> 00:12:40.450
- I sure hope not.
- I hope not.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:41.703
- No, they couldn't.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:45.040
Richard Ramirez is dead, right?

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.737
- As far as we know, yes.
- Is he dead, Ryan?

00:12:46.737 --> 00:12:48.107
- He's a ghost now.
- Think he died in 2013.

00:12:48.107 --> 00:12:50.350
- Okay.
- Oh, okay.

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:51.530
Well, that's good for us then.

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:53.130
- It's good for everyone.
- Yeah.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:55.130
- In a world where maybe there would be

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:56.890
other real life serial killers,

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:58.160
do you guys have one that you,

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:00.450
maybe Shane you have
one that you wanna see?

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.940
- Ideally, you would want someone

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:05.350
who you don't really wanna glorify them,

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:06.740
and if you could take a little

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:09.660
liberties with them,
then obviously Zodiac,

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.137
'cause Ryan Murphy can be like

00:13:11.137 --> 00:13:14.370
"Well, dream up some
little story about Zodiac,"

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:15.590
'cause nobody knows who he is.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:16.750
Sure, bring him into the picture.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:17.730
- That is true.
- Right.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.360
- Are there other shows out there

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.480
that you think our friends
at home should watch

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.900
if they're loving "1984" right now?

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:27.110
- I mean, all I can
think of is "The Terror,"

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:30.790
in the sense that each season
is kind of its own story.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:33.470
It's not quite as fun and light-hearted.

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:37.210
But it's a different take each season

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:40.620
on sort of a thematically
similar horror story

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.080
rooted in history.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.870
- It's kind of hard to think
of a high quality serialized

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:47.820
piece of content that is as campy as this,

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.120
in the horror genre.
- Right, yeah.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:49.953
- Maybe "Dark."

00:13:49.953 --> 00:13:51.690
"Dark" is also set in the '80s,

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:53.930
kind of, for the majority
of the first season.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.130
It's a German horror show,

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:57.350
but I enjoyed that. I think it's very fun.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.300
- It's a good German "Stranger Things."

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:01.760
- It's only like "Stranger
Things" in the sense

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.640
that a kid goes missing
and that's about it.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:06.840
- But there's like an
element of a town ecosystem.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:08.000
- That is true.
- And some kind of

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.077
overarching mystery.

00:14:09.077 --> 00:14:10.672
- "Santa Clarita Diet."

00:14:10.672 --> 00:14:11.505
- I haven't seen that.
- Ohh.

00:14:11.505 --> 00:14:13.180
- If someone has not watched that show,

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:15.080
that show is hands down
one of the best things

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.010
Netflix has ever made.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:17.720
Drew Barrymore and Tim Olyphant--

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:18.830
- So good.
- I like Tim, Tim's great.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:20.070
- are phenomenal in it.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:23.220
But that's like a perfect
blend of horror comedy

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:26.000
and just the extremes
they go to with the gore,

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:26.877
but how charming that family is.

00:14:26.877 --> 00:14:28.540
- Yeah.
- I feel like,

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.520
I don't know, that's
just the perfect marrying

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.860
of blood and gore, but also
really charming content.

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:35.240
- I agree.
- I have to check that out.

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:36.073
- I love that one.

00:14:36.073 --> 00:14:38.400
Also, have you guys heard of
"Two Sentence Horror Stories"

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:39.233
on Netflix?

00:14:39.233 --> 00:14:40.066
- No.
- No.

00:14:40.066 --> 00:14:40.899
- [Perri] I have heard of that.

00:14:40.899 --> 00:14:43.640
- It aired on the CW in August,
and now it's on Netflix,

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:46.520
But it's also horror
anthology, 30 minute episodes.

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:47.353
I love it.

00:14:47.353 --> 00:14:48.320
- It's on my list.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.060
- Yeah, and 'cause they
really take everything we love

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:51.770
about horror but put a modern twist on it.

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.450
You guys would love it. It's so funny.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:57.440
All right guys, let's talk
theories now, finally.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:58.280
- Oh, no.
- Who do we think

00:14:58.280 --> 00:14:59.440
the last camper's gonna be?

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.850
What do we think is gonna happen?

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:02.499
Perri, I feel like you
have a lot of theories

00:15:02.499 --> 00:15:03.500
you're gonna drop on us.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.860
- I have so many theories,

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.820
and with every single theory that I like,

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:08.450
I can always find one or two points

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:09.490
that make it not possible.

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:11.400
But, the main thing that I latched onto

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:12.233
right from the start

00:15:12.233 --> 00:15:14.750
was the idea that it is basically a movie

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:16.920
being made within the series.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:18.750
I mean, just look at the opening credits.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.370
It all takes place kind of on a TV screen,

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:23.080
and even at the end of those credits,

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.145
when the tapes are being shown.

00:15:25.145 --> 00:15:25.978
- Yeah.
- Oh, yeah.

00:15:25.978 --> 00:15:28.340
- The tape fizzles out
of it, I don't know.

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:29.540
So many things point to that,

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:33.037
and then the very first time
the hiker says to someone

00:15:33.037 --> 00:15:34.550
"You're not supposed to be here,"

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:37.620
it made me think that
someone popped up in a scene

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:38.670
when they weren't.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.830
- [Naz] Yeah, he says "I'm
not supposed to die here."

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:41.663
- [Perri] Yeah.

00:15:41.663 --> 00:15:44.030
- It's with Richard Ramirez
and I was like is this a game?

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:48.020
- Maybe Richard Ramirez
walks into the filming

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:50.950
of a horror movie and
he's caught off guard.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.457
- That's interesting because when he said

00:15:52.457 --> 00:15:53.700
"I'm not supposed to be here"

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:55.160
I just figured it was
a ghost going through

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:57.080
a residual haunting,
like living the same day

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.660
over and over and over again.
- Well, to be fair,

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.040
the hiker is one of the
things that does not

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:02.940
entirely work in the TV idea

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.970
because I do think the hiker is a ghost,

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:07.293
and that's where I get
to the hellmouth theory.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:09.740
- What is the hellmouth theory?

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:10.850
- So they exist.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:15.850
I think they exist in
"Murder House," Hotel Cortez,

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.850
and maybe here too,

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:20.420
where when people die in
a particular location,

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:22.300
they're dead, but they're never gone.

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:24.040
So if the hiker is stuck there,

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:26.460
and who knows, maybe Leslie
Grossman is stuck there.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.700
Maybe she really died
at the very beginning

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:31.710
and she's another individual like him,

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.006
and she's just stuck there.

00:16:33.006 --> 00:16:35.170
- Ryan, Shane, what are your theories?

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:36.130
- That movie theory's really good.

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:38.960
I do think that Emma is
going to be the villain

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:40.530
at the end of the show.

00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:42.810
- But then, isn't that so obvious?

